module alsd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.states.alabama.{ frcp6-alabama }

// The Southern District of Alabama's own periods and page limits,
// computed under the federal rules (FRCP 6(a) governs "any local rule").
// The briefing periods of CivLR 7 and 56 apply "unless the Court orders
// otherwise", and the court may set different motion and summary
// judgment practice in a case (CivLR 7(i), 56(f)). Rules that state no
// period or limit stay out: individual judges' procedures (GenLR 1.1),
// serving and filing (GenLR 5), requests for court action (GenLR 7),
// witnesses, jury instructions and places of trial (GenLR 43, 51, 77),
// magistrate judges' duties (GenLR 73), decorum, appearances and pro se
// parties (GenLR 83.1, 83.2, 83.5), forms, the effective date and
// bankruptcy reference (GenLR 84, 86, 87), commencing an action (CivLR
// 3), discovery filings (CivLR 5), pleading (CivLR 8, 9), pro se Rule 12
// motions (CivLR 12), discovery (CivLR 26-37), consolidation (CivLR 42),
// sureties (CivLR 65.1) and the registry (CivLR 67, 67.1). Unsealing on
// a criminal indictment or complaint (GenLR 5.2(d)(3), (4)) and the
// criminal peremptory challenge request (GenLR 47(d)) are criminal
// rules; the admission and discipline periods of GenLR 83.3 and 83.4
// govern attorneys, not a civil action; neither is encoded. The court's
// own power to dismiss when a served defendant has not answered within
// six months of the complaint (CivLR 41(b)) sets no party's deadline and
// stays in this note. Periods in business days, a unit lit/core does not
// count, stay in notes: the balance of a bid over $1,000.00 within three
// business days (CivLR 104(m)(2)(B)), an objection to a sale within
// three business days following it (CivLR 104(m)(6)) and the appraiser's
// one business day's notice (CivLR 104(i)). The notices CivLR 102(b)(5)
// and (6) prescribe restate Supplemental Rule C(6), FRCP authority, and
// are not re-encoded. Amounts are not declared: the supersedeas bond of
// the judgment plus 15% and $500.00 (CivLR 62(a)), security for costs of
// $500.00 (CivLR 65.2, 104(g)) and $1,000.00 (CivLR 105(a)), and the
// bid deposit (CivLR 104(m)(2)). The earlier S.D. Ala. outline's FRCP and
// FRAP flow and its decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Celotex, Anderson v.
// Liberty Lobby, Matsushita, Unitherm, Bowles v. Russell, Hamer,
// Microsoft v. Baker, and Khalik v. United Air Lines, a Tenth Circuit
// decision it misattributed to this circuit) are FRCP and FRAP authority
// and belong to lit/frcp and lit/frap; they are removed here: no reporter
// text is vendored.
/// A principal brief in support of, or in opposition to, a motion: at
/// most 30 pages, excluding the caption, cover page, tables and signature
/// block, absent prior leave (CivLR 7(e)).
limit principal-brief { pages <= 30 cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 7(e)" } cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 7(e)"
/// A reply brief: at most 15 pages, with the same exclusions, absent
/// prior leave (CivLR 7(e)).
limit reply-brief { pages <= 15 cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 7(e)" } cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 7(e)"

/// A notice of supplemental authority: at most 2 pages, presenting no new
/// argument (CivLR 7(f)(3)).
limit supplemental-authority-notice {
  pages <= 2 cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 7(f)(3)"
} cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 7(f)(3)"

/// An order sealing a document not otherwise listed in GenLR 5.2(d) is
/// entered (GenLR 5.2(d)(5)).
event SealingOrderEntered()
/// An objection to a magistrate judge's determination is served (GenLR
/// 72(c)).
event MagistrateObjectionServed()
/// A response to the objection is served (GenLR 72(c)(3)).
event MagistrateObjectionResponseServed()
/// A party receives a court file, exhibit, document or transcript on an
/// order allowing its temporary withdrawal (GenLR 79(d)).
event FileWithdrawn()
/// A trial is concluded, by verdict, mistrial, settlement or otherwise
/// (GenLR 79(f)(1)).
event TrialConcluded()
/// A case is concluded, by judgment, order of dismissal or otherwise
/// (GenLR 79(f)(1), (2)).
event CaseConcluded()
/// The judgment becomes final (GenLR 79(f)(3)(A)).
event JudgmentFinal()
/// The complaint is filed (CivLR 4(a)(3)).
event ComplaintFiled()
/// Service is completed by summons (CivLR 4(a)(1)).
event ServiceCompleted()
/// The plaintiff receives a waiver of service (CivLR 4(a)(2)).
event WaiverReceived()
/// A motion other than one under FRCP 56 is served (CivLR 7(c)).
event MotionServed() paper principal-brief
/// The non-movant's response to that motion is served (CivLR 7(d)).
event ResponseServed() paper principal-brief
/// A reply brief is filed (CivLR 7(d), (e)).
event ReplyFiled() paper reply-brief
/// A notice of pertinent and significant authority is filed (CivLR
/// 7(f)(3)).
event SupplementalAuthorityNoticed() paper supplemental-authority-notice
/// A party's initial filing is made without its Disclosure Statement,
/// filing it being impossible or impracticable (CivLR 7.1(a)).
event InitialFilingMade()
/// The complaint of a plaintiff proceeding under a pseudonym is served
/// (CivLR 10(c)).
event PseudonymousComplaintServed()
/// The court grants a motion to amend a pleading (CivLR 15(c)).
event AmendmentGranted()
/// The final pretrial conference is held (CivLR 16(c)(1)).
event FinalPretrialConference()
/// The case is referred to early neutral evaluation (CivLR 16(d)(4)(B)).
event EneReferred()
/// Judgment is entered (CivLR 54(a)(1)).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// The order resolving a timely FRCP 50(b) or 59 motion is entered (CivLR
/// 54(a)(1)).
event PostTrialMotionResolved()
/// A verified bill of costs is served (CivLR 54(a)(3)).
event BillOfCostsServed()
/// Objections to the bill of costs are served (CivLR 54(a)(3)).
event CostsObjectionsServed()
/// The clerk taxes costs (CivLR 54(b)).
event CostsTaxed()
/// A motion for summary judgment is served (CivLR 56(b)).
event SummaryJudgmentMotionServed() paper principal-brief
/// The non-movant's response to the summary judgment motion is served
/// (CivLR 56(c)).
event SummaryJudgmentResponseServed() paper principal-brief
/// The Rule C(3)(c) summons to show cause is served on the person having
/// control of intangible property (CivLR 102(a)).
event IntangibleSummonsServed()
/// Property is seized in an action in rem (CivLR 102(b)).
event PropertySeized()
/// An order to post security for costs under Rule E(2)(b) is entered
/// (CivLR 104(g)).
event SecurityOrderEntered()
/// The Marshal requests that the seizing party advance additional sums
/// (CivLR 104(j)).
event MarshalAdvanceRequested()
/// Property is sold in an action in rem (CivLR 104(m)).
event SaleHeld()
/// The court confirms the sale (CivLR 104(m)(2)(C)).
event SaleConfirmed()

/// GenLR 5.2(d)(5): unless the court orders otherwise, other sealed
/// documents are unsealed 120 days from the date of entry of the sealing
/// order.
deadline unsealing-period: 120.days after SealingOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. GenLR 5.2(d)(5)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// GenLR 72(c)(2): where the parties have not consented to magistrate
/// judge jurisdiction, any other party may serve and file a response to an
/// objection within fourteen days from the date of service of the
/// objection, unless the court sets a different deadline.
deadline magistrate-objection-response-period: 14.days after MagistrateObjectionServed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. GenLR 72(c)(2)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// GenLR 72(c)(3): unless the court orders otherwise, the objecting party
/// may serve and file a reply within seven days from the date of service
/// of the response.
deadline magistrate-objection-reply-period: 7.days after MagistrateObjectionResponseServed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. GenLR 72(c)(3)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// GenLR 79(d): a party granted temporary withdrawal returns the court
/// file, exhibit, document or transcript within seven days, unless the
/// judge by order sets a different time.
deadline file-return-period: 7.days after FileWithdrawn() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. GenLR 79(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// GenLR 79(f)(1): within fourteen days after a trial is concluded, the
/// offering party withdraws all exhibits in the clerk's custody.
deadline exhibit-withdrawal-period: 14.days after TrialConcluded() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. GenLR 79(f)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// GenLR 79(f)(1): within fourteen days after a case is concluded, the
/// offering party withdraws all discovery material in the clerk's custody.
deadline discovery-withdrawal-period: 14.days after CaseConcluded() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. GenLR 79(f)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// GenLR 79(f)(2): exhibits and discovery material not withdrawn within
/// sixty days after a case is concluded may be disposed of by the clerk.
deadline exhibit-disposal-period: 60.days after CaseConcluded() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. GenLR 79(f)(2)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// GenLR 79(f)(3)(A): a party retains exhibits and discovery material
/// withdrawn from the clerk's custody for at least one year after the
/// judgment is final.
deadline exhibit-retention-period: 1.years after JudgmentFinal() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. GenLR 79(f)(3)(A)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 4(a)(1): unless the court orders otherwise, if service is
/// completed by summons, the person making service files proof of it
/// within seven days of the date of service.
deadline proof-of-service-period: 7.days after ServiceCompleted() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 4(a)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 4(a)(2): if service is waived, the plaintiff files the waiver
/// within seven days after receipt of the waiver.
deadline waiver-filing-period: 7.days after WaiverReceived() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 4(a)(2)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 4(a)(3): if within forty-five days after the filing of the
/// complaint the plaintiff has neither completed service by summons nor
/// received a waiver, the plaintiff files a notice describing its efforts
/// to complete service and their results.
deadline service-attempt-notice-period: 45.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 4(a)(3)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 7(c): unless the court orders otherwise, the non-movant files
/// any brief or paper in opposition to a motion, other than one under FRCP
/// 56, within fourteen days of service of the motion.
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 7(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 7(d): unless the court orders otherwise, a reply in support of a
/// motion, other than one under FRCP 56, is filed within seven days of
/// service of the non-movant's response.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after ResponseServed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 7(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 7.1(a): where filing the Disclosure Statement with the initial
/// filing is impossible or impracticable, it is filed within seven days
/// after the initial filing, or such other time as the court directs.
deadline disclosure-statement-period: 7.days after InitialFilingMade() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 7.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 10(c): a party who commences a civil action under a pseudonym
/// files and serves a motion for permission to proceed under it within
/// twenty-one days of service of the complaint.
deadline pseudonym-motion-period: 21.days after PseudonymousComplaintServed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 10(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 15(c): if a responsive pleading is required, a party that has
/// appeared and was served with the proposed amended pleading serves its
/// answer or other responsive pleading within fourteen days after the
/// court grants the motion to amend.
deadline amended-pleading-response-period: 14.days after AmendmentGranted() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 15(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 16(c)(1): unless otherwise ordered, the parties file a joint
/// pretrial document seven days before the final pretrial conference.
deadline joint-pretrial-document-period: 7.days before FinalPretrialConference() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 16(c)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 16(d)(4)(B): within thirty days of the case being referred to
/// ENE, the neutral evaluator hosts the confidential evaluation meeting.
deadline ene-session-period: 30.days after EneReferred() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 16(d)(4)(B)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 54(a)(1): no later than fourteen days after entry of judgment, a
/// party seeking costs files a verified bill of costs. Absent court order,
/// an appeal does not extend the deadline (CivLR 54(a)(2)).
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 14.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 54(a)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 54(a)(1): if a timely FRCP 50(b) or 59 motion is filed, the bill
/// of costs is filed within fourteen days after entry of the order
/// resolving the motion.
deadline bill-of-costs-post-motion-period: 14.days after PostTrialMotionResolved() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 54(a)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 54(a)(3): a party opposing taxation of costs files its
/// objections within fourteen days of service of the bill of costs.
deadline costs-objection-period: 14.days after BillOfCostsServed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 54(a)(3)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 54(a)(3): the party claiming costs serves any response within
/// seven days of service of the objections.
deadline costs-objection-response-period: 7.days after CostsObjectionsServed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 54(a)(3)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 54(b): a party may move for review of the clerk's taxation of
/// costs no later than seven days after taxation.
deadline costs-review-period: 7.days after CostsTaxed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 54(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 56(b): unless the court orders otherwise, the non-movant files
/// any response in opposition to a summary judgment motion within
/// twenty-eight days of service of the motion.
deadline summary-judgment-response-period: 28.days after SummaryJudgmentMotionServed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 56(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 56(c): unless the court orders otherwise, any reply is filed
/// within fourteen days of service of the non-movant's response.
deadline summary-judgment-reply-period: 14.days after SummaryJudgmentResponseServed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 56(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 102(a): the Rule C(3)(c) summons directs the person having
/// control of intangible property to show cause no later than fourteen
/// days after service why it should not be delivered to the court; a
/// judicial officer may lengthen or shorten the time.
deadline intangible-show-cause-period: 14.days after IntangibleSummonsServed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 102(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 102(b): the Rule C(4) notice, published once a week for three
/// consecutive weeks, begins not later than twenty-one days following
/// seizure.
deadline arrest-notice-period: 21.days after PropertySeized() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 102(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 104(g): a party ordered to post security for costs posts it
/// within seven days after the order is entered; a party who fails to may
/// not participate further except by order of court.
deadline admiralty-security-period: 7.days after SecurityOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 104(g)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 104(j): the Marshal may, on notice, petition for an order to
/// release the vessel if additional sums are not advanced within seven
/// days after the Marshal's request.
deadline marshal-advance-period: 7.days after MarshalAdvanceRequested() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 104(j)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 104(m)(1): unless otherwise ordered, the last publication of the
/// notice of sale is not less than seven days immediately preceding the
/// sale.
deadline sale-notice-period: 7.days before SaleHeld() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 104(m)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 104(m)(2)(C): if an objection to the sale is timely filed, the
/// bidder is excused from paying the balance of the purchase price until
/// five days after the sale is confirmed.
deadline objected-sale-balance-period: 5.days after SaleConfirmed() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 104(m)(2)(C)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// CivLR 104(m)(7): if no objection is timely filed, the sale is
/// confirmed by order no sooner than five days and no later than seven
/// days after the sale.
deadline sale-confirmation-period: 7.days after SaleHeld() counted_by frcp6-alabama cite "S.D. Ala. CivLR 104(m)(7)"
{
  forum frcp
}
